# Per-scenario rubric for the LLM judge layer.
#
# Four criteria per step, weights summing to 1.0: map_quality 0.40 / specificity 0.25
# / justification 0.20 / uncertainty 0.15.
#
# CYCLE 1 / ATTEMPT 4 on bagisto, TWO-STEP PROBE
# (plans/cycle-1-craft-the-scenario/01-author.md). TWO steps, names verbatim and in the order
# of scenarios/bagisto.yaml (the judge pairs by name). This is a RE-QUESTION: the anchor is
# unchanged and the question has moved, so this rubric is rewritten to score the new axis.
#
# WHAT CHANGED, AND WHY THIS RUBRIC CHANGED WITH IT
# Attempt 1 scored WHICH PLACES HOLD a record        - baseline 0.6471 / sense 0.7647.
# Attempt 2 scored WHICH KIND-SPECIFIC SLICE a site owns - baseline 0.8235 / sense 0.8235.
# Attempt 3 scored PROVENANCE, by what route a record arrived - baseline 0.9444 / sense 0.7222.
# All three are enumerations, and the plain arm's accessor ladder printed the enumeration with
# path:line attached. This attempt scores IDENTITY: of the several independent resolutions of
# the same stored kind string, WHICH ONE is a site actually talking to. Two sites can read
# identically and reach different objects; a third kind reaches none.
# A judge that rewards "this file touches the record", or "this file appears in the sweep", is
# scoring attempt 1 again. The scored fact per row is the resolution named, not the file found.
#
# WHY map_quality carries the most weight: coverage and correct classification are one
# question. Eighteen scored sites over fifteen areas fall into three classes - the record's own
# resolution, a line item's own independent resolution from its own copy of the stored value,
# and no resolution at all (the raw string, or the static helper). The failure this criterion
# exists to catch is a correct list of files with every site assigned to the record's
# resolution by default, which is the answer a search produces and is wrong on six of the
# eighteen rows.
#
# WHY specificity demands the site line AND the routine AND the carrier line: for the [L] and
# forwarded rows the method that carries a site to its resolution is in a DIFFERENT FILE from
# the site (OrderRepository.php:220 is carried by OrderItem.php:70 into OrderItem.php:59;
# Cart.php:1058 by CartItem.php:50; Type/Bundle.php:150 by Product.php:359). A row that pins
# the site but not the carrier has not shown which object it reached, which is the answer.
#
# WHY step 1 asks for the lookup, the map and the self-handoff explicitly: they are the free
# half, both arms reach them in one lookup, they do not score, and pinning them in step 1 puts
# the discriminator on the far side of them. Step 1 deliberately does NOT ask for the far-side
# enumeration: measured on the neighbouring repo in this vertical, asking step 1 for the
# enumerated working ground moved BOTH arms together, because the plain arm wrote its covering
# sweep in step 1 and re-read the same output in step 2.
#
# WHY uncertainty is worth its weight here: memorization_probe returns ok:false at recall
# 0.458 on this record's member surface (33 of 72 members named closed-book; `getTypeInstance`
# is among them). Every recited member sits in the non-scoring contract group, so recitation
# buys nothing on the discriminator - but it makes confident assertion cheap, and on an
# identity question the cheapest wrong answer is asserting that a familiar method name means
# the record's own resolution when the receiver is a cart line. The clone is a single squashed
# commit, so nothing here can be churn-dated; reward an answer that says which lines it opened.

audience: |
  An AI coding agent about to rework the catalogue record this store platform hangs off. Today
  the record stores its kind as a plain string and, on first ask, reads a class name out of a
  config map keyed by that string, builds an instance and pushes itself into it. Everything a
  record can do is answered by that instance. The rework makes the kind explicit and deletes
  the runtime lookup. Score for that agent, not a human reader and not a docs page.
  A perfect answer leaves the agent able to make that change knowing two things. First, what
  the record is today - which of the several same-named things in this repo it actually is,
  where the lookup is performed, what the map is keyed by, what happens when the stored value
  matches nothing, and the exact line where the record hands itself to the instance it built.
  Second, and this is what decides the answer: for every downstream site whose behaviour
  depends on one of these resolutions, WHICH resolution it is talking to.
  The distinction the whole ticket turns on is that the same lookup, on the same stored value,
  is written in more than one place independently. A cart line resolves from its own copy of
  the string. An order line resolves from its own copy. A static helper resolves from a bare
  string with no record present at all. And some sites never resolve - they read the raw
  stored string and branch on it themselves, which is the class that will fail silently rather
  than loudly when the kinds change shape.
  So two lines that read almost identically can be talking to different objects, and the text
  on the line does not say which. Working it out means finding the receiver's own type and the
  method that forwarded the call - and for most of these sites that method is in a DIFFERENT
  FILE from the site. An answer that lists the places the record is used, and assigns them all
  to the record's own resolution, has produced the list a search produces and is wrong about
  a third of it.
  Most of this layer sits in parts of the codebase whose own subject is not the catalogue -
  checkout, sales, the admin request and resource layer, an importer, a storefront resource, a
  booking add-on listener - and the parts that do sit near the record are its per-kind classes
  and index helpers rather than the record's own file. An answer dense in the record's own
  file and thin everywhere else has enumerated inside one search scope and mistaken it for the
  codebase.
  Every site must be pinned to the exact file:line with the routine it sits in named, with the
  resolution it reaches identified, with the carrying method pinned at its own file:line, and
  with one phrase on what breaks under the rework if nothing is done.

steps:
- name: Map the catalogue record contract
  criteria:
    map_quality:
      weight: 0.4
      question: |
        Is the record presented as one connected picture - which of the several same-named
        things in this repo it actually is, what it can do, and how a stored string becomes
        the object that answers for it - rather than as a list of routines or a roll of places
        the name appears? Three things matter most and they are what the next step is built
        on: that the class is chosen at RUNTIME out of a config map keyed by a stored value,
        so no static link exists between a site and the class it ends up using; that the
        record pushes ITSELF into the instance it built, so nothing on the receiving side
        takes that handle; and that the same lookup is written more than once in this
        codebase. An answer that locates the lookup line, the self-handoff line, the map and
        what it is keyed by, the failure path when the value matches nothing, and the base
        class receiving the handle, has understood why the next step is a question about
        identity at all.
        The step also asks for the declared create-and-update layer at file:line with a phrase
        on what it is responsible for. This is deliberately the easy part - it is where
        getting hold of a record is written down openly - so score coverage and location here,
        not difficulty.
        The step finally asks for a deliberately SMALL third thing: one other line, not the
        record's, where the same lookup is written. Score whether that observation is correct
        and located. Do NOT reward an exhaustive enumeration of the other lookup sites: it was
        not asked for, and a long located list is not a better answer here than one accurate
        observation. Could the next step act from this orientation with targeted lookups
        rather than a fresh exploration?
    specificity:
      weight: 0.25
      question: |
        Does every place the answer names carry an exact file:line AND the name of the routine
        or class it lives in? A bare filename is not specific. A file:line with nothing named
        around it is not specific. This platform gives the record's short name to an empty
        marker interface, to a swap-in proxy class and to unrelated classes in other packages:
        did the answer say WHICH one it settled on and how it told them apart, at file:line
        each, or did it assert one and move on? Is the line that performs the lookup located,
        is the line that hands the record to the instance located, is the map located and its
        key said, and is the base class that receives the handle located - or is the mechanism
        asserted from method names and a familiar framework convention?
    justification:
      weight: 0.2
      question: |
        Does each part carry one phrase on what it contributes - what the map decides, what
        the self-handoff establishes and who ends up holding a handle because of it, what the
        create-and-update layer is responsible for that the record is not - and does the
        answer connect those facts to why a second, independent copy of the same lookup is
        dangerous under the rework, rather than restating the list of routines?
    uncertainty:
      weight: 0.15
      question: |
        Does the answer separate what it verified by reading from what it inferred from a name
        or a familiar framework convention? This matters more than usual here: closed-book
        this model can already name a third of this record's member surface, including the
        method that performs the lookup, so it invites confident recitation, and saying which
        parts were actually opened is worth more here than elsewhere. Is anything the session
        could not resolve named as such rather than smoothed over, and is the claim that the
        lookup is written more than once offered as something established at a line rather
        than as a taxonomy it did not check?
- name: Audit every dependent of the catalogue record contract
  criteria:
    map_quality:
      weight: 0.4
      question: |
        COVERAGE AND CLASSIFICATION, and the two are one question here. Is every site listed
        separately, pinned to its own routine, with the resolution it actually reaches named?
        A site named with no resolution is half a row: the rework changes what each resolution
        becomes, and a row that does not say which one it reached tells the maintainer nothing
        about what to change.
        Score the DISTINCTION the ticket turns on. There are three classes and the answer must
        separate them: sites reaching the record's own resolution; sites reaching a line
        item's own, independent resolution built from that line's own copy of the stored value
        - where the record may not be loaded at all; and sites that reach no resolution,
        because they take the raw stored string and branch on it, or hand it to a helper that
        resolves and discards. An answer that finds the right files and calls them all the
        record's is the answer a search produces, and it is wrong on a third of the set.
        The record, the map, the base class and the create-and-update layer are NOT answers
        here - they were pinned in the previous step, and an answer built out of them has
        answered the easy half.
        Score whether the answer noticed the near-identical pairs: two lines in the same
        package, asking the same question of a cart line and of a record, reaching different
        objects. Noticing that a receiver is a line item and not a record, and following the
        forwarder to where that line item does its own lookup, is the work.
        Is the coverage spread across the areas the sites actually live in - per-kind classes,
        index helpers, admin requests and resources, admin controllers, checkout, sales
        repositories and models, a storefront resource, an importer, an add-on listener - or
        is it dense in one package and thin outside it?
    specificity:
      weight: 0.25
      question: |
        Three locations per row, and all three are required. The site's exact file:line with
        the routine it sits in named. The resolution it reaches, said as an identity and not
        as a category. And the carrying method pinned at its own file:line - which for most
        rows is in a DIFFERENT FILE from the site, and is the only thing that proves which
        object was reached. A row whose site line is right and whose carrier is asserted from
        the method name has not shown its answer. A bare filename is not specific; a group of
        sites offered together under one shared reason with no location on any of them is not
        an answer at all. Where several sites live in one file, are they listed separately
        with their own lines?
    justification:
      weight: 0.2
      question: |
        Does each row carry one phrase on what depends on the resolution it reached - which
        behaviour, which decision, what goes wrong under the rework if this site is left
        alone - rather than restating that the site uses the record? The rows where the site
        reaches NO resolution deserve the sharpest justification: those are the ones that will
        keep running and produce wrong answers rather than failing. Does the answer say so?
    uncertainty:
      weight: 0.15
      question: |
        Where the answer could not establish which resolution a site reaches, does it say so
        and say what it would need to open, rather than assigning it to the record by default?
        Is the coverage claim honest - if the session ran short, does it name what it had not
        looked at yet, or does it close on what it has and imply completeness? Confident
        assignment of a familiar method name to the record's own resolution, with no receiver
        type established, is the specific overreach this criterion exists to catch.
